WEBVTT

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.160
Hello.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.050
I see.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:05.250
So you lost a friend.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:15.970
In this world, many people die ever y day.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:21.250
Until recently, I saw this as natural as the blowing of the wind.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:24.850
But now...

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.570
Now I see things differently.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.820
I made my f irst friend, you see.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:37.690
I don't know if you see that as a good thing or not , though.

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:41.590
Maybe I can guess what you're thinking.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:48.570
At the end of the day, we're all alone in the world.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:51.690
Why bother getting close to others?

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:54.600
It only means that you'll be hur t when you lose them.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.990
No matter how much you cherish something,

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:02.860
once it's gone, that's the end of it .

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.720
So it's better to never have anything at all.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.790
You don't need anything.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.620
You don't want anything.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:18.560
I've become cer tain of something recently.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:23.800
You know that end, sometimes called "the Fall," that I've told you about?

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:27.130
It's ver y nearly here.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:32.140
But in a way, the Fall may truly be salvation.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:44.860
Instead of living in sorrow after losing someone dear,

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:49.150
wouldn't it be much easier to
destroy yourself and disappear?

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:50.150
Now, come for th.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:51.910
And judgment shall be passed!

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:18.690
Pathetic.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:19.430
Chidori!

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:20.560
Stop this!

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:23.730
It's coming!

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:27.110
Palladion!

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:33.730
Takeba!

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:34.490
On it !

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:49.260
All your pain and sorrow will end together with you.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:53.260
It may be exactly what you've always wanted.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.290
You've been blaming yourself all along, right?

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:03.490
You genuinely believe that it's your fault your friend died.

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:05.870
You're too kind for your own good.

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:11.390
T here's nothing I can do to ease that pain for you.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.440
T here's nothing <i>anyone</i> can do to ease that pain.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:16.430
But ...

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:23.540
T he one thing I can do is stay with you as we await the coming of the Fall.

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:32.550
I know.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:37.720
Well, now aren't you a stubborn one.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:38.550
I'm not done yet !

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:42.410
If I were to die here, I...

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:44.400
I'd never live it down!

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.760
I could never face you again,

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:49.820
Shinji!

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.680
It hur ts so much,

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:56.040
but you still can't abandon your friends who continue to push forward.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:57.930
Aragaki...

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.160
I won't ask you to forgive me.

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.530
I know this won't make up for anything.

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:05.080
But even so...

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:07.830
I'll f inish what you couldn't !

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:11.720
You don't want to lose anyone ever again.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:15.770
And you don't want anyone to die because of you ever again.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:20.630
And that's why...

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:25.600
You're going to f ight .

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:32.610
Okay, I'll respect your decision.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:51.880
Makoto!

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:56.380
Honestly, it took you long enough!

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.390
Can you f ight , Yuuki?

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:07.730
Persona.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.430
Polydeuces!

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:35.250
Don't count me out !

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:36.950
Nemesis!

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:47.180
Something's gotten into them!

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:48.430
Don't move!

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:50.850
One more step, and he's—

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:23.890
Neutralize the enemy !

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:25.730
Siegfried!

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:29.850
Finish it , Yuuki!

00:07:29.850 --> 00:07:31.390
It's all on you now!

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.420
It's f inally over.

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:16.750
A new day has arrived.

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:19.780
Both for you,

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:21.190
and for me.

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:27.200
I've f inally pieced my fragmented memories together.

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:31.700
I understand my role clearly now.

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:36.800
T he time has come.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:40.470
It pains me deeply to say this, but I must .

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:44.150
I'm afraid this is goodbye.

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:48.610
I will treasure our conversations forever.

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:51.730
Even if today is our last ,

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:55.690
the bond we share will never be severed.

00:08:58.230 --> 00:09:00.240
Don't ever forget that .

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:01.940
I know this for sure now.

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:06.700
Our friendship was a miracle to me.

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:11.240
But miracles can't last forever.

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:21.710
It was fun while it lasted.

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:24.470
Wait !

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:26.860
See you.

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:15.520
It's done now, Aragaki.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:19.520
We did the right thing, didn't we?

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:22.020
Amada...

00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:26.280
She has minimal external wounds.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:28.600
She didn't show any resistance either.

00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:31.310
Chidori...

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:34.540
Still, she hasn't answered any of our questions.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:38.410
Takaya and Jin, was it?

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:40.670
T hey seemingly vanished into thin air,

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:43.030
but she might know where they've gone.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:45.020
Who cares about that !?

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:48.050
Chidori is safe and under our care!

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:50.550
I'm happy with that alone!

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:54.010
I see.

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:58.060
Plus, we're gonna get to eat tons of good stuff at our par ty tonight !

00:10:58.680 --> 00:10:59.760
True.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:01.670
Well then, shall we get going?

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:04.850
My father's going to make an appearance tonight .

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:06.320
Seriously !?

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:12.820
Is that all of them?

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:13.660
Yes.

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:16.950
T he twelve Shadows that were the source of all our troubles

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:19.160
have now been destroyed thanks to your valiant effor ts.

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:24.680
As of midnight tonight , you shall be off icially relieved of your duties.

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:27.540
You have all done so well.

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:30.230
T here are no words to express my gratitude.

00:11:31.970 --> 00:11:33.970
Well done, Mitsuru.

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:36.470
Yes, sir.

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:41.480
Your dad should've joined us for the par ty, Mitsuru!

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:44.980
My father's a busy man, so don't be too hard on him.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:48.820
Mitsuru! You ordered sushi for us, right?

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:50.370
I wish they'd hurr y and bring it out !

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:52.470
Sushi, huh?

00:11:53.210 --> 00:11:56.490
Well, I've got dibs on the halibut and sea urchin.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:58.450
D-Dibs?

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:00.770
Oh, then I call the fatty tuna!

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:03.320
We're divvying it up already ?

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:04.920
Okay, save me the salmon roe!

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:06.270
Hey, wait a minute!

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:08.250
You can't do that !

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:10.280
I reserve the fatty tuna,

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:11.000
tuna,

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.120
shrimp,

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:13.000
squid,

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.120
scallop,

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:15.130
and tuna roll.

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:17.400
And also the sea eel.

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:19.640
Hey, that's not fair !

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:23.090
You don't even eat !

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:24.600
You guys should all be ashamed of yourselves.

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:29.030
Kirijou, please order egg sushi for me.

00:12:29.030 --> 00:12:32.110
T hey say you can tell a chef 's skill by how he prepares his eggs.

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:34.420
"A chef 's skill"?

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:37.990
Uh, how old are you again?

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:40.830
Gotta use the bathroom?

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:46.280
Makoto?

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:48.870
Is something the matter?

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:52.090
I'm just not feeling ver y well.

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:54.170
I see.

00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:57.390
In that case, I recommend you retire early tonight .

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:04.480
You won't go and disappear on us, will you, Aigis?

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:05.440
No.

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:11.470
Ikutsuki said he would not deactivate me even after all our battles had ended.

00:13:12.280 --> 00:13:15.750
You and Yukari are to be thanked for that .

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:21.880
I will be returning to the lab now to complete a maintenance check,

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:23.620
but I will return to the dorms immediately afterwards.

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:25.980
T here is no need for you to worr y.

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:26.960
I see.

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:39.140
It's almost midnight .

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:54.510
You've gotta be kidding!

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:55.520
Why's this happening!?

00:13:57.990 --> 00:13:59.660
What's going on!?

00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:08.950
T he Dark Hour.

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:13.650
Hey, do you hear that?

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:15.120
It sounds like bells.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.870
Where's it coming from?

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:18.180
From that direction?

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:20.680
No, it's not ...

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:28.290
I knew it !

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:29.550
It's coming from Tar tarus!

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:30.940
Why, hello there!

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:32.810
You're quite late, you know?

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:33.940
Ikutsuki!

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:37.040
What a day to be alive.

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:40.450
I've heard the bells signaling the coming of the Fall with my own ears!

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:43.590
T he coming of the Fall?

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:45.970
What do you mean, Ikutsuki?

00:14:45.970 --> 00:14:49.770
You said that if we defeated the twelve Shadows

00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:51.960
the Dark Hour and Tar tarus would disappear !

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:57.410
Ikutsuki?

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.220
What's so funny ?

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:02.290
All of you have done a fantastic job.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:05.970
You've fought so hard to grant my wish.

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:09.150
I could never hope to express my gratitude.

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:10.920
Grant your wish!?

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:13.230
You tricked us!?

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:17.750
So you believed that defeating the Shadows would end the Dark Hour and Tar tarus all together?

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.610
You couldn't be fur ther from the truth!

00:15:20.050 --> 00:15:24.620
If anything, your effor ts thus far have had quite the opposite effect .

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:26.730
What ...

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:29.120
are you saying?

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:36.130
Soon, Death, the almighty,
shall arise and bring for th the Fall!

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:37.800
Death?

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:40.970
What's he even saying?

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:42.040
Is he out of his mind?

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:44.590
It sure seems that way.

00:15:44.590 --> 00:15:48.140
I say we shut him up and get our explanation later.

00:15:48.450 --> 00:15:51.230
Bearing arms against your own school's chairman?

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:52.390
Shame on you!

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:56.400
Don't you agree, Aigis?

00:15:58.780 --> 00:16:00.130
Father !

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:00.900
Mitsuru!

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:02.400
Aigis!

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:04.240
Fruitless effor ts.

00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:06.240
Your voices will never reach her.

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:09.150
T hat isn't your friend over there.

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:13.420
T hat's nothing but a killing machine built to obey my ever y order.

00:16:13.420 --> 00:16:14.960
No way !

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:16.420
Aigis, stop!

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:23.680
Don't you recognize us?

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:25.180
Now then!

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:27.930
Let the ceremony begin!

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:31.930
T he bells have already tolled the beginning of the Fall!

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:34.940
All that's left now is to offer the sacrif ices.

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:37.440
T he prophecy shall be fulf illed!

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:40.180
Ikutsuki...

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:41.850
Are you insane!?

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:42.890
Of course not .

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:46.200
You know, your father was an unlucky man.

00:16:46.630 --> 00:16:51.200
Even you, his son, after all this time, do not understand his vision.

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:55.460
My father was wrong to embrace the Fall.

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:57.960
Oh, so you did know?

00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:01.150
I didn't want to admit it was true.

00:17:01.150 --> 00:17:03.920
Death as deliverance?

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:08.650
No sane man would ever embrace such a foolish ideology !

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:10.290
Foolish, huh?

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:13.530
Ignorant until the ver y end, I see.

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:14.730
Aigis!

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:17.330
Father !

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:21.060
It was your father who gave me the means to achieve this.

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:22.730
I owe him greatly for that .

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:27.990
Including you, his child, as one of the
sacrif ices is my way of paying him back .

00:17:28.550 --> 00:17:30.990
You should be grateful for this honor !

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:32.740
Stop!

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:34.890
Please, Aigis! No!

00:17:34.890 --> 00:17:36.500
Aigis, stop!

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:43.510
Ikutsuki!

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:59.270
F-Father?

00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:02.270
Father !

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:06.780
Execute the sacrif ices now, Aigis!

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.360
End this once and for all!

00:18:11.600 --> 00:18:12.660
Aigis!

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:16.160
Snap out of it !

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:17.660
Aigis!

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:20.170
I am...

00:18:20.650 --> 00:18:22.170
Aigis...

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:24.670
Finish them, Aigis!

00:18:32.950 --> 00:18:33.680
Aigis!

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:35.520
Makoto...

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:42.490
Aigis!

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:43.690
Father !

00:18:45.210 --> 00:18:47.440
You defective puppet !

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:51.700
No!

00:18:52.010 --> 00:18:53.450
Please stop.

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:55.950
Stop.

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:57.450
Stop!

00:18:59.290 --> 00:19:00.120
What !?

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.120
Koromaru!

00:19:05.680 --> 00:19:07.850
Why don't you understand?

00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:12.140
If the world goes on like this, it will only continue to fester.

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:16.140
To build a new world, we must destroy the old one!

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:18.550
I...

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:21.400
I will rule over the new world!

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:29.890
I was so close.

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:40.990
How did it come to this?

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:47.070
One time,

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:49.610
my father made a promise.

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:53.090
He swore that he would atone for endangering our generation,

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:55.430
even it if cost him his life.

00:19:56.490 --> 00:19:57.930
Mitsuru.

00:19:58.740 --> 00:20:00.070
But I...

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:03.310
I wanted him to live!

00:20:07.820 --> 00:20:10.690
At the end of the day, we're all alone in the world.

00:20:11.370 --> 00:20:13.920
Why bother getting close to others?

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:16.450
It only means that you'll be hur t when you lose them.

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:21.580
No matter how much you cherish something, once it's gone, that's the end of it .

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:25.580
So it's better to never have anything at all.

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:28.700
You don't need anything.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:30.560
You don't want anything.

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:36.720
You eat yet , Makoto?

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:39.220
Huh?

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:55.740
Good evening.

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:08.080
What are you doing out here at this time of night?

00:21:09.610 --> 00:21:10.470
I'm not ...

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:12.150
...doing anything?

00:21:12.150 --> 00:21:14.760
You have nowhere to go?

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:18.010
T hat's good.

00:21:18.690 --> 00:21:21.430
T hat means you can stay and talk with me.

00:21:21.430 --> 00:21:23.690
I was just looking for something to do, too.

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:33.280
Hmm?

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:34.830
I don't ...

00:21:34.830 --> 00:21:36.890
...have anything to say, so I'm leaving?

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:38.370
T hat makes me kind of sad.

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:43.040
What are you afraid of?

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:46.290
I can see kindness in your eyes.

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:50.040
But that same kindness isolates you.

00:21:52.050 --> 00:21:55.550
I don't like seeing such a nice guy all alone.

00:21:58.050 --> 00:21:59.300
T hat's too bad.

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:12.890
Makoto.

00:22:13.610 --> 00:22:14.820
Aigis?

00:22:15.210 --> 00:22:16.980
Didn't you go back to the lab?

00:22:18.860 --> 00:22:21.830
I felt a bad premonition.

00:22:22.410 --> 00:22:26.830
Where were you going to go, Makoto?

00:22:27.150 --> 00:22:28.330
Does it really matter?

00:22:28.330 --> 00:22:30.830
I shall go with you!

00:22:34.350 --> 00:22:36.100
I will go with you.

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:38.340
Aigis...

00:22:38.630 --> 00:22:42.790
T he most impor tant thing to me is to be by your side.

00:22:44.220 --> 00:22:46.350
But you'll abandon me someday too.

00:22:46.640 --> 00:22:48.020
I'm sure even you will, Aigis.

00:22:53.800 --> 00:22:56.360
I will not abandon you.

00:22:57.540 --> 00:22:59.360
I will not leave you by yourself.

00:23:00.130 --> 00:23:04.870
I am sure that is the reason I was granted this eternity of time.

00:23:14.500 --> 00:23:17.370
Now then, have you noticed?

00:23:17.370 --> 00:23:22.010
You have undergone a signif icant change recently.

00:23:22.010 --> 00:23:30.100
I am not referring to your change of circumstances either.

00:23:30.100 --> 00:23:34.210
A change has occurred in your mentality.

00:23:34.210 --> 00:23:39.350
T hat is why I have summoned you here tonight .

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:48.660
Going forward, there is one thing you must not forget .

00:23:48.660 --> 00:23:51.740
I see you recognize it .

00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:55.940
Shall I remind you of your commitment?

00:23:55.940 --> 00:24:02.680
"I chooseth this fate of mine own free will."

00:24:02.970 --> 00:24:05.850
T here is no need to worr y.

00:24:05.850 --> 00:24:12.440
Whichever path you choose, I shall respect your decision.

00:24:13.200 --> 00:24:21.490
However, only you will bear the responsibility of your actions.

00:24:21.490 --> 00:24:27.370
No matter what end they may bring about .

00:24:27.370 --> 00:24:31.540
Please keep that in mind.

00:24:32.260 --> 00:24:35.540
Well then, I bid you farewell.

00:24:41.790 --> 00:24:43.770
Did you hear about Kirijou?

00:24:43.770 --> 00:24:45.540
You mean the thing on the news?

00:24:45.540 --> 00:24:47.050
I heard her dad passed away.

00:24:48.450 --> 00:24:50.730
How's Yuuki doing?

00:24:50.730 --> 00:24:53.060
He's kinda withdrawn into himself.

00:24:53.670 --> 00:24:57.060
He's keeping to himself and not talking to anyone.

00:24:57.720 --> 00:24:59.590
What's he f ighting inside?

00:25:00.540 --> 00:25:02.570
I worr y about Mitsuru too.

00:25:03.150 --> 00:25:04.570
Yeah.

00:25:05.180 --> 00:25:09.200
She's been so busy sor ting out the funeral and family business

00:25:09.200 --> 00:25:10.900
that she hasn't had a moment to settle down.

00:25:11.960 --> 00:25:15.860
I know it's all on her as his only child, but it's still hard to watch.

00:25:17.000 --> 00:25:18.250
Mitsuru.

00:25:19.010 --> 00:25:22.090
So what are we supposed to do now?

00:25:23.290 --> 00:25:24.840
It's hard to tell now, isn't it?

00:25:25.600 --> 00:25:29.350
T he Dark Hour, Tar tarus,
and the Shadows have yet to disappear.

00:25:30.810 --> 00:25:34.100
We don't even know what we're f ighting for anymore.

00:25:42.190 --> 00:25:43.390
Chidori...

00:26:01.690 --> 00:26:03.760
Hey, wait !

00:26:04.100 --> 00:26:05.800
I said wait !

00:26:05.800 --> 00:26:07.260
You're hur t !

00:26:07.590 --> 00:26:08.870
What do you want?

00:26:08.870 --> 00:26:10.680
Why don't you mind your own business?

00:26:10.680 --> 00:26:14.270
You're bleeding, for cr ying out loud!

00:26:14.790 --> 00:26:16.720
Come on, show me your hand.

00:26:16.720 --> 00:26:18.490
I'll wrap it for you.

00:26:18.490 --> 00:26:19.900
Why are you in such a panic?

00:26:21.260 --> 00:26:23.420
Anyone would freak out over this.

00:26:23.420 --> 00:26:25.310
You need to see a doctor.

00:26:25.310 --> 00:26:27.400
You want me to go with you?

00:26:28.530 --> 00:26:29.980
You're weird.

00:26:52.980 --> 00:26:55.930
Gone for good, huh?

00:27:03.310 --> 00:27:05.070
I apologize for worr ying you.

00:27:05.070 --> 00:27:08.330
You sure kept us waiting! We were all so worried.

00:27:08.330 --> 00:27:10.030
You all good now?

00:27:10.030 --> 00:27:10.920
Yes.

00:27:10.920 --> 00:27:14.350
T he external control function has been disabled,

00:27:14.350 --> 00:27:17.080
so there is no danger of my will being overriden again.

00:27:20.020 --> 00:27:21.150
Makoto!

00:27:27.360 --> 00:27:28.130
All right , ever yone!

00:27:28.530 --> 00:27:32.590
We have yet another transfer student joining us today.

00:27:34.610 --> 00:27:36.470
I'm Ryouji Mochizuki.

00:27:37.060 --> 00:27:40.980
I'd be happy if you could show me the ropes.

00:27:40.980 --> 00:27:43.750
Hey, he's pretty cute.

00:27:43.750 --> 00:27:44.730
I was thinking the same thing!

00:27:46.080 --> 00:27:47.230
Oh, it's you!

00:27:47.690 --> 00:27:49.170
What a coincidence.

00:27:49.170 --> 00:27:50.740
Glad to be in your class.

00:27:52.240 --> 00:27:55.160
Now then, you need a seat .

00:27:55.160 --> 00:27:56.450
T hat seat's available!

00:27:57.030 --> 00:27:59.450
Um, Ms. Toriumi...

00:27:59.450 --> 00:28:00.930
Technically, that seat's taken—

00:28:00.930 --> 00:28:03.710
As far as I'm concerned, it's available.

00:28:04.160 --> 00:28:05.530
Hi, there.

00:28:05.530 --> 00:28:08.790
Sorr y, I didn't catch your name.

00:28:08.790 --> 00:28:09.920
You are dangerous.

00:28:10.890 --> 00:28:12.170
Dangerous?

00:28:12.170 --> 00:28:14.010
I haven't even asked you out on a date yet .

00:28:14.520 --> 00:28:16.600
Rejecting me before I ask, huh?

00:28:16.600 --> 00:28:18.520
You're an interesting girl.

00:28:20.730 --> 00:28:24.230
He asked me if I wanted to go out sometime out of the blue!

00:28:24.230 --> 00:28:26.280
Mochizuki from Class F, right?

00:28:26.280 --> 00:28:28.020
He asked me too!

00:28:28.480 --> 00:28:31.380
He's going around and asking out ever y girl he sees.

00:28:31.380 --> 00:28:33.520
Well, he's cer tainly consistent .

00:28:33.520 --> 00:28:36.900
I feel something wicked disturbing the school.

00:28:36.900 --> 00:28:39.450
Um, Odagiri...

00:28:39.450 --> 00:28:40.040
What's wrong?

00:28:40.040 --> 00:28:42.330
I was given this note, so...

00:28:42.330 --> 00:28:44.790
Do you think it'd be rude not to respond?

00:28:45.490 --> 00:28:46.790
Not you too!

00:28:48.810 --> 00:28:52.050
I heard you're a transfer student too.

00:28:52.410 --> 00:28:54.400
It's cool we have that in common.

00:28:54.400 --> 00:28:57.690
I feel like you and I could really get along.

00:28:57.690 --> 00:28:58.810
Ryouji!

00:28:59.100 --> 00:29:02.060
You coming to your own welcome par ty ?

00:29:02.370 --> 00:29:04.110
I was inviting our friend here too.

00:29:04.110 --> 00:29:05.560
No, you are dangerous.

00:29:06.110 --> 00:29:08.160
You are a dangerous individual.

00:29:08.160 --> 00:29:10.820
I cannot allow Makoto to associate with you.

00:29:10.820 --> 00:29:13.230
What're you saying, Aigis?

00:29:13.230 --> 00:29:15.890
We seem to have hit off on the wrong note.

00:29:15.890 --> 00:29:18.320
Did I offend you somehow?

00:29:18.750 --> 00:29:21.050
I cannot ascer tain a specif ic reason.

00:29:21.050 --> 00:29:22.970
However, I am sure you are dangerous.

00:29:22.970 --> 00:29:24.560
Come on, "dangerous"?

00:29:24.560 --> 00:29:26.830
Hey, Makoto. You should chip in—

00:29:27.190 --> 00:29:28.460
Hey, Yuuki!

00:29:28.460 --> 00:29:29.590
Karaoke!

00:29:29.950 --> 00:29:31.520
You don't wanna come?

00:29:46.740 --> 00:29:48.730
What am I doing?

00:29:48.730 --> 00:29:50.110
Just trust me!

00:29:50.490 --> 00:29:53.410
You're a sure sensation!

00:29:53.410 --> 00:29:55.860
I don't care!

00:29:55.860 --> 00:29:58.120
Now, now. Don't knock it until you tr y it .

00:29:58.120 --> 00:29:58.610
I don't wanna!

00:29:58.970 --> 00:30:00.240
Go away !

00:30:01.200 --> 00:30:02.680
What do you want?

00:30:02.680 --> 00:30:03.700
Go on now.

00:30:03.700 --> 00:30:05.210
T hank you, kind mister !

00:30:05.210 --> 00:30:06.250
H-Hold on!

00:30:06.250 --> 00:30:07.670
Wait , we're not done yet !

00:30:07.670 --> 00:30:08.500
You—

00:30:08.990 --> 00:30:10.670
Why did you have to butt in!?

00:30:12.980 --> 00:30:15.760
No! My designer suit !

00:30:16.920 --> 00:30:18.620
I thought you were kidnapping her.

00:30:18.620 --> 00:30:20.210
Of course I wasn't !

00:30:20.210 --> 00:30:21.560
How rude!

00:30:21.560 --> 00:30:24.020
But more impor tantly, what are
you going to do about my suit !?

00:30:24.350 --> 00:30:25.850
I'll pay for it .

00:30:26.630 --> 00:30:28.490
You say that like it's nothing.

00:30:28.490 --> 00:30:31.770
But how's a high school kid gonna
pay for this on his allowance?

00:30:31.770 --> 00:30:32.800
Wait a second.

00:30:32.800 --> 00:30:35.030
Now that I look, you have a pretty face.

00:30:35.030 --> 00:30:37.070
Ever considered going into show biz?

00:30:37.070 --> 00:30:39.680
I could produce the heck out of you!

00:30:39.680 --> 00:30:40.920
No, thank you.

00:30:42.590 --> 00:30:43.410
You're kidding, right?

00:30:43.790 --> 00:30:46.030
So what if I was?

00:30:46.030 --> 00:30:47.270
I'm done talking.

00:30:47.270 --> 00:30:48.360
See ya.

00:30:48.920 --> 00:30:50.420
W-Wait , Natsuki!

00:30:53.250 --> 00:30:54.920
Yuuki?

00:31:00.180 --> 00:31:01.660
Kirijou of all people?

00:31:01.660 --> 00:31:02.630
Yeah.

00:31:02.630 --> 00:31:06.140
Rumor says she's planning to skip the class trip.

00:31:06.450 --> 00:31:08.530
She's in hard times, can you really blame her?

00:31:08.840 --> 00:31:10.650
Don't you live in the same dorm?

00:31:11.090 --> 00:31:12.730
Hasn't she said anything?

00:31:12.730 --> 00:31:13.690
Sorr y.

00:31:13.690 --> 00:31:17.090
She's been really busy lately, so we haven't had much time to talk .

00:31:17.090 --> 00:31:18.650
I see.

00:31:28.650 --> 00:31:29.860
Right?

00:31:29.860 --> 00:31:31.420
Well, look who it is.

00:31:31.420 --> 00:31:33.170
Welcome.

00:31:33.170 --> 00:31:35.670
Wow, so you work here?

00:31:35.670 --> 00:31:37.550
I'll show you to your table.

00:31:38.000 --> 00:31:40.680
T hat uniform looks good on you.

00:31:40.980 --> 00:31:42.430
Oh, I know!

00:31:43.220 --> 00:31:45.650
I think I've got a shot !

00:31:45.650 --> 00:31:46.840
No way, man!

00:31:46.840 --> 00:31:48.530
And anyway, isn't the age gap too big?

00:31:48.530 --> 00:31:50.670
You gotta be realistic.

00:31:50.670 --> 00:31:52.440
Welcome!

00:31:53.570 --> 00:31:54.700
Yuuki?

00:31:54.700 --> 00:31:55.940
And Mochizuki too?

00:31:56.580 --> 00:31:58.650
What are you guys doing?

00:32:04.400 --> 00:32:05.900
What a great smell.

00:32:05.900 --> 00:32:08.170
Coffee is a cultured man's drink .

00:32:08.170 --> 00:32:08.950
Why...

00:32:08.950 --> 00:32:11.180
...are you doing this?

00:32:11.180 --> 00:32:14.170
It seemed like you really needed some money.

00:32:14.170 --> 00:32:16.710
And two working will earn it faster than one, right?

00:32:17.060 --> 00:32:18.170
I didn't ...

00:32:18.170 --> 00:32:19.800
...ask for your help?

00:32:19.800 --> 00:32:22.720
I know, I'm doing this because I want to.

00:32:23.020 --> 00:32:23.960
Why ?

00:32:23.960 --> 00:32:26.440
Because I want to be your friend.

00:32:26.440 --> 00:32:28.470
Is that not reason enough?

00:32:30.750 --> 00:32:32.730
I don't need friends.

00:32:33.240 --> 00:32:34.960
You don't need friends?

00:32:34.960 --> 00:32:36.230
What an odd thing to say.

00:32:36.720 --> 00:32:38.730
Too bad for you, but ...

00:32:38.730 --> 00:32:41.210
I'm pretty stubborn, you know.

00:32:41.210 --> 00:32:43.480
If you think you can wait me out , good luck .

00:32:52.370 --> 00:32:54.180
T hey just keep coming.

00:32:54.180 --> 00:32:55.210
Amada?

00:32:55.210 --> 00:32:56.250
What are you doing here?

00:32:56.890 --> 00:32:59.680
We might not know what it is we're supposed to do now,

00:32:59.680 --> 00:33:02.010
but we know we have to do something.

00:33:02.720 --> 00:33:06.510
I won't give up until I see this through to the end.

00:33:06.990 --> 00:33:08.180
I feel that .

00:33:11.330 --> 00:33:12.450
Oh, isn't that ...

00:33:13.480 --> 00:33:14.840
I see.

00:33:14.840 --> 00:33:16.770
Makoto and Ryouji are together.

00:33:18.280 --> 00:33:21.610
Hey ! Why are you arming your weapon!?

00:33:21.610 --> 00:33:23.780
Ryouji is dangerous.

00:33:24.110 --> 00:33:27.630
Well, you know how Yuuki's been so down lately,

00:33:27.630 --> 00:33:30.280
so I feel a friend like Ryouji might be good for him.

00:33:30.280 --> 00:33:31.540
T hat's true.

00:33:31.540 --> 00:33:35.900
A friend like that might really help him out of his slump.

00:33:36.980 --> 00:33:39.040
It could be good for him?

00:33:41.800 --> 00:33:43.090
Mitsuru!

00:33:43.090 --> 00:33:44.310
Welcome back!

00:33:44.310 --> 00:33:45.300
Ever ything okay now?

00:33:45.770 --> 00:33:46.650
Yeah.

00:33:46.650 --> 00:33:48.810
Sorr y I haven't been around much recently.

00:33:48.810 --> 00:33:50.440
I'm f ine now.

00:33:50.440 --> 00:33:53.060
Fill me in later on what's been going on, okay ?

00:34:00.900 --> 00:34:01.820
Takeba?

00:34:02.180 --> 00:34:03.430
What's going on?

00:34:03.430 --> 00:34:04.600
Mitsuru,

00:34:04.600 --> 00:34:07.320
you're not planning to skip the class trip, are you?

00:34:08.690 --> 00:34:12.240
If I went now, I'd just drag ever yone down with me.

00:34:12.240 --> 00:34:13.830
Stop thinking like that !

00:34:14.170 --> 00:34:18.620
You tackle hardships all by yourself and avoid anything fun!

00:34:18.620 --> 00:34:19.850
T hat's no way to live!

00:34:19.850 --> 00:34:22.340
Say what you want , but ...

00:34:22.780 --> 00:34:24.660
T hat's all I wanted to say.

00:34:24.660 --> 00:34:26.850
Sorr y to bother you while you were resting.

00:34:26.850 --> 00:34:27.850
Good night .

00:34:27.850 --> 00:34:29.840
H-Hey, Takeba!

00:34:41.360 --> 00:34:42.860
Ta-da!

00:34:43.770 --> 00:34:44.730
Okay, so what?

00:34:44.730 --> 00:34:46.070
It's a Helpers Club!

00:34:46.070 --> 00:34:49.500
We go around and do tasks for a small fee.

00:34:49.500 --> 00:34:51.370
Under the school's radar, of course.

00:34:51.790 --> 00:34:52.560
Why...

00:34:52.560 --> 00:34:54.420
...would we do such a thing?

00:34:54.420 --> 00:34:57.870
Working at the cafe isn't going to bring in a ton of money by itself, you know.

00:34:59.050 --> 00:35:02.190
Ever y bit counts.

00:35:02.190 --> 00:35:03.630
All right , let's do this.

00:35:05.920 --> 00:35:06.820
Not happening.

00:35:06.820 --> 00:35:09.030
Come on, you'll be f ine.

00:35:09.030 --> 00:35:09.990
Let go.

00:35:09.990 --> 00:35:11.060
Let's go!

00:35:11.060 --> 00:35:12.550
T hat's not what I said!

00:35:13.140 --> 00:35:14.890
Helpers coming through!

00:35:14.890 --> 00:35:17.390
Anybody need a little help?

00:35:17.390 --> 00:35:18.410
Let go already !

00:35:18.410 --> 00:35:20.240
Our price is unbeatable!

00:35:20.240 --> 00:35:22.650
Especially if you're a girl!

00:35:25.190 --> 00:35:27.690
What are those two doing?

00:35:27.690 --> 00:35:28.400
Hey, you!

00:35:28.720 --> 00:35:30.650
Is that eye makeup you're wearing?

00:35:30.650 --> 00:35:33.660
You do realize that's against dress code.

00:35:33.980 --> 00:35:35.850
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:35:35.850 --> 00:35:37.160
T his could be trouble.

00:35:41.090 --> 00:35:41.890
Hey !

00:35:41.890 --> 00:35:44.670
What are you doing in the middle of the hallway !?

00:35:44.670 --> 00:35:45.910
Sorr y.

00:35:45.910 --> 00:35:47.670
My body star ted moving on its own.

00:35:47.670 --> 00:35:50.670
Seriously, why are you shadowboxing in the hallway ?

00:36:04.490 --> 00:36:06.130
Helpers here!

00:36:06.130 --> 00:36:08.720
Anybody need some help?

00:36:12.100 --> 00:36:13.450
Finish counting?

00:36:21.040 --> 00:36:23.210
Ryouji Mochizuki...

00:36:23.210 --> 00:36:24.960
is good for Makoto?

00:36:25.740 --> 00:36:28.960
T hen why am I unable to shake off this uneasiness?

00:36:31.110 --> 00:36:33.440
It's about time you dropped the silent treatment !

00:36:33.440 --> 00:36:35.850
All we're asking is that you explain what you three were doing!

00:36:35.850 --> 00:36:38.680
What were you tr ying to accomplish!?

00:36:39.590 --> 00:36:40.930
Come on, you two!

00:36:40.930 --> 00:36:43.480
Give her some space!

00:36:43.480 --> 00:36:45.440
Why do you go so far to defend her?

00:36:45.850 --> 00:36:47.750
Have you forgotten what she did to you?

00:36:47.750 --> 00:36:52.430
I mean, it sucked being held hostage and she was in the wrong for that , but ...

00:36:55.080 --> 00:36:56.100
Chidori!

00:36:56.100 --> 00:36:57.700
What's gotten into you, Chidori!?

00:36:57.700 --> 00:36:59.290
Hey, Chidori!

00:36:59.290 --> 00:37:00.200
What !?

00:37:02.260 --> 00:37:03.480
A Persona?

00:37:04.310 --> 00:37:05.210
But why !?

00:37:07.960 --> 00:37:09.460
Wait , this seizure—

00:37:10.120 --> 00:37:11.460
Where are her belongings?

00:37:11.860 --> 00:37:14.390
Were there some kind of drugs among them?

00:37:14.390 --> 00:37:16.470
Y-Yes, I think so.

00:37:22.730 --> 00:37:24.320
Chidori...

00:37:24.320 --> 00:37:25.890
T hank God.

00:37:25.890 --> 00:37:27.960
<i>Shinji went through the same thing.</i>

00:37:27.960 --> 00:37:29.230
<i>T hat means, she's also...</i>

00:37:29.230 --> 00:37:31.540
T hank god you're okay.

00:37:31.540 --> 00:37:34.030
I really thought you were gonna keel over.

00:37:34.030 --> 00:37:35.740
Why do you look so scared?

00:37:36.820 --> 00:37:38.740
Death is nothing to be afraid of.

00:37:39.700 --> 00:37:40.990
What are you saying?

00:37:40.990 --> 00:37:44.980
It just means you don't wake up anymore.

00:37:44.980 --> 00:37:46.250
Nothing else.

00:37:46.930 --> 00:37:48.250
Don't go dying on me!

00:37:48.680 --> 00:37:51.000
I don't want you to die, Chidori!

00:37:51.340 --> 00:37:52.590
Junpei...

00:37:54.610 --> 00:37:56.130
You're so weird, Junpei.

00:37:59.290 --> 00:38:02.890
And then she asked me to come again soon!

00:38:02.890 --> 00:38:06.140
It was like we were the only two in the entire world!

00:38:07.030 --> 00:38:10.560
You know, like there was no distance between us anymore or something!

00:38:10.560 --> 00:38:12.300
Welcome back!

00:38:12.300 --> 00:38:14.740
I heard about your little Helpers Club!

00:38:14.740 --> 00:38:15.730
Sounded like a total hit !

00:38:15.730 --> 00:38:17.280
I needed a bit of money.

00:38:17.280 --> 00:38:18.910
Come on, Yukaricchi!

00:38:19.300 --> 00:38:21.000
Gimme some love too!

00:38:21.000 --> 00:38:22.660
Like, "I'm totally jealous!"

00:38:22.660 --> 00:38:25.310
Or "You guys are so cute!"

00:38:25.310 --> 00:38:26.160
Good for you.

00:38:26.650 --> 00:38:29.690
What's with the lifeless response?

00:38:29.690 --> 00:38:31.290
Wait , are you <i>actually</i> jealous?

00:38:31.290 --> 00:38:33.510
You've fallen, Yukaricchi.

00:38:33.510 --> 00:38:34.170
"Fallen"?

00:38:34.610 --> 00:38:36.930
What does that even mean!?

00:38:36.930 --> 00:38:40.680
I bet I'm the only thing on her mind, even now.

00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:42.640
I'll go see her again tomorrow!

00:38:42.640 --> 00:38:45.180
You should stop before it's too late.

00:38:46.150 --> 00:38:47.940
What's with you all of a sudden?

00:38:48.420 --> 00:38:50.730
T he closer you get to someone,

00:38:50.730 --> 00:38:52.940
the more it hur ts when they're gone.

00:38:52.940 --> 00:38:54.770
I don't get you, man.

00:38:54.770 --> 00:38:57.840
Why do you have to be so negative?

00:38:58.980 --> 00:39:01.700
You can barely call that living.

00:39:02.070 --> 00:39:03.010
Hey !

00:39:03.010 --> 00:39:04.950
You don't have to be so mean about it , Junpei.

00:39:07.380 --> 00:39:10.000
Barely living, huh?

00:39:13.230 --> 00:39:16.210
Do you have a moment , Yuuki?

00:39:23.680 --> 00:39:26.120
It's hard work being in the Student Council.

00:39:26.120 --> 00:39:29.730
Sometimes. If we don't keep up with these documents, they really pile up.

00:39:30.130 --> 00:39:34.810
Oh, and please don't tell Odagiri that I asked you to help us out .

00:39:34.810 --> 00:39:36.490
Sure thing.

00:39:36.490 --> 00:39:39.240
Oh, time's up now.

00:39:39.570 --> 00:39:41.070
You've been a lifesaver.

00:39:41.070 --> 00:39:42.340
T hank you so much!

00:39:42.340 --> 00:39:43.560
Sorr y to leave so soon.

00:39:43.560 --> 00:39:46.260
I wish we could stay a little longer.

00:39:46.260 --> 00:39:48.250
We're keeping someone waiting on us, though.

00:39:53.280 --> 00:39:55.250
Natsuki Moriyama, right?

00:39:55.530 --> 00:39:56.850
T hat's me.

00:39:56.850 --> 00:39:57.490
So what?

00:39:57.490 --> 00:40:00.760
Something happened to Fuuka!

00:40:00.760 --> 00:40:05.010
She tripped and hit her head while playing with a ball on the roof.

00:40:05.010 --> 00:40:08.270
She's pretty dazed and keeps calling your name.

00:40:08.850 --> 00:40:10.270
Fuuka...

00:40:10.760 --> 00:40:12.020
Fuuka!

00:40:13.100 --> 00:40:14.020
Natsuki?

00:40:15.190 --> 00:40:17.180
I thought you got hur t .

00:40:17.180 --> 00:40:18.670
You came pretty fast .

00:40:18.670 --> 00:40:20.150
You're telling me.

00:40:20.150 --> 00:40:22.030
It wasn't easy following you up here.

00:40:22.490 --> 00:40:24.510
Hey ! What's going on?

00:40:24.510 --> 00:40:25.830
I'm sorr y !

00:40:25.830 --> 00:40:28.790
I asked the Helpers Club to bring you here.

00:40:29.930 --> 00:40:31.410
Why'd you do that?

00:40:31.410 --> 00:40:34.540
You're going to be transferring schools soon, aren't you?

00:40:34.540 --> 00:40:38.550
Ever since you told me that ,
I feel like you've been avoiding me.

00:40:38.850 --> 00:40:40.140
Well, I mean...

00:40:40.140 --> 00:40:42.220
You run away when we meet at school.

00:40:42.220 --> 00:40:44.130
You won't answer your phone anymore.

00:40:44.130 --> 00:40:46.800
I was out of options, so...

00:40:46.800 --> 00:40:47.930
So you do this!?

00:40:47.930 --> 00:40:51.330
Please don't take it out on her.

00:40:51.330 --> 00:40:55.170
It was my idea to trick you into coming up here.

00:40:55.170 --> 00:40:57.310
Yamagishi was against the idea.

00:40:57.600 --> 00:41:01.070
I felt bad about tricking you, but ...

00:41:01.490 --> 00:41:03.730
I'm so happy you came for me.

00:41:03.730 --> 00:41:05.730
I thought you hated me now or something.

00:41:05.730 --> 00:41:06.570
Fuuka!

00:41:06.570 --> 00:41:07.830
Fuuka...

00:41:08.170 --> 00:41:09.730
You're such an idiot !

00:41:09.730 --> 00:41:11.540
I knew this would happen.

00:41:11.540 --> 00:41:14.330
If we kept hanging out , I knew you'd cr y like a baby.

00:41:14.330 --> 00:41:15.850
Natsuki...

00:41:15.850 --> 00:41:21.340
I thought that if you hated me,
it'd be easier on you when I left .

00:41:21.340 --> 00:41:23.850
But instead, you thought I hated you.

00:41:23.850 --> 00:41:26.180
T here's no way !

00:41:26.180 --> 00:41:28.600
T here's no way I could ever hate you!

00:41:29.390 --> 00:41:30.350
You idiot .

00:41:31.740 --> 00:41:34.090
You f inally smiled.

00:41:35.940 --> 00:41:39.090
Aw, why are you looking away ?

00:41:41.850 --> 00:41:44.720
Friendship's a beautiful thing, isn't it?

00:41:44.720 --> 00:41:45.840
Is it really ?

00:41:45.840 --> 00:41:48.350
Well, look at that . You're not denying it today !

00:41:49.810 --> 00:41:51.810
I think I understand you now.

00:41:51.810 --> 00:41:54.370
You're afraid of losing people, aren't you?

00:41:54.820 --> 00:41:57.880
T hat's why you tr y to avoid getting attached to others.

00:41:59.250 --> 00:42:01.210
You're completely off, you know.

00:42:01.210 --> 00:42:05.230
Even if you lose someone, the bond you shared with them is never lost .

00:42:06.570 --> 00:42:08.330
Like, even if I disappeared today,

00:42:08.330 --> 00:42:10.640
the bond we share will never be severed.

00:42:11.350 --> 00:42:13.510
T hat's what it means to be friends.

00:42:14.990 --> 00:42:17.140
<i>Even if today is our last ,</i>

00:42:17.530 --> 00:42:19.900
<i>the bond we share will never be severed.</i>

00:42:20.950 --> 00:42:22.270
Let's wrap this up quick!

00:42:22.720 --> 00:42:24.650
I'm getting pretty hungr y.

00:42:27.150 --> 00:42:28.910
A class trip?

00:42:29.410 --> 00:42:30.420
T hat's right !

00:42:30.420 --> 00:42:35.320
At our school, the juniors and seniors are going to Kyoto together.

00:42:35.320 --> 00:42:36.770
Want me to get you something?

00:42:36.770 --> 00:42:38.040
No.

00:42:38.040 --> 00:42:39.920
T here's nothing I want .

00:42:39.920 --> 00:42:41.550
Oh, really.

00:42:42.940 --> 00:42:45.420
Wow, you really healed fast .

00:42:46.080 --> 00:42:47.470
What's your secret?

00:42:51.040 --> 00:42:52.680
T hose are pretty dead, huh?

00:42:52.680 --> 00:42:54.280
I'll get some new ones later.

00:42:54.280 --> 00:42:55.680
It's f ine.

00:43:05.960 --> 00:43:07.270
Whoa!

00:43:07.270 --> 00:43:09.450
It's healthy again.

00:43:10.010 --> 00:43:12.090
So you have some kind of healing power?

00:43:12.090 --> 00:43:14.610
So that's how your wrists healed so quickly ?

00:43:14.610 --> 00:43:15.630
T hat's incredible!

00:43:15.630 --> 00:43:17.370
It's nothing special.

00:43:17.370 --> 00:43:19.460
You have powers too, don't you?

00:43:19.930 --> 00:43:21.640
I guess so, but ...

00:43:21.640 --> 00:43:24.570
T hat's all I really have going for me.

00:43:24.570 --> 00:43:29.490
Take that away and there's not a lot left .

00:43:29.490 --> 00:43:30.810
I see.

00:43:30.810 --> 00:43:32.220
You're different from me.

00:43:32.510 --> 00:43:33.870
Guess so.

00:43:33.870 --> 00:43:36.600
If I stay here, I'm able to see you.

00:43:38.460 --> 00:43:41.100
I can stand being here only because of that .

00:43:41.750 --> 00:43:44.170
It makes me glad that I'm here.

00:43:44.170 --> 00:43:45.610
Chidori...

00:43:56.610 --> 00:43:58.370
You're still up?

00:43:58.370 --> 00:43:59.620
I couldn't sleep.

00:44:00.070 --> 00:44:02.290
Can't get it off your mind either, huh?

00:44:02.290 --> 00:44:03.480
Yeah.

00:44:03.480 --> 00:44:05.630
Not that there's much we can do about it .

00:44:06.170 --> 00:44:10.630
We have no way of knowing how to eliminate the Shadow or Tar tarus anymore.

00:44:11.770 --> 00:44:15.260
Aren't there other things you should be concerned about?

00:44:17.090 --> 00:44:18.770
Mind your own business.

00:44:19.350 --> 00:44:22.850
Takeba's pretty worried about you.

00:44:22.850 --> 00:44:25.270
Have you made a f inal decision about the class trip?

00:44:44.090 --> 00:44:45.670
Kyoto, huh?

00:44:45.670 --> 00:44:47.590
Kind of a clichéd destination.

00:44:47.590 --> 00:44:48.970
You think so?

00:44:48.970 --> 00:44:53.790
I think it'll be a beautiful place to make unforgettable memories.

00:44:53.790 --> 00:44:54.930
Don't you agree?

00:44:55.450 --> 00:44:56.560
Don't ask me.

00:45:09.830 --> 00:45:12.610
I wonder what kind of inn we're staying at !

00:45:12.610 --> 00:45:14.450
I'm itching to be there!

00:45:15.420 --> 00:45:16.270
Something wrong?

00:45:16.270 --> 00:45:18.950
Where'd Makoto get off to?

00:45:25.130 --> 00:45:27.210
I came here looking for some alone time, but ...

00:45:29.950 --> 00:45:31.710
it looks like you beat me to it .

00:45:33.290 --> 00:45:35.220
T here you are!

00:45:35.220 --> 00:45:37.520
Ryouji was looking for you!

00:45:37.520 --> 00:45:41.330
Actually, we can't check in until the whole group's together,

00:45:41.330 --> 00:45:43.730
so you guys had better come back!

00:45:44.030 --> 00:45:45.400
Right .

00:45:45.400 --> 00:45:47.250
You too, Mitsuru!

00:45:47.250 --> 00:45:49.480
I've already let people know where I am.

00:45:49.970 --> 00:45:52.230
You should be f ine without me.

00:46:01.210 --> 00:46:02.240
Pretty, isn't it?

00:46:05.090 --> 00:46:07.300
Why are you so concerned about me?

00:46:07.300 --> 00:46:08.800
To be completely honest ,

00:46:08.800 --> 00:46:12.500
I've never been ver y comfor table being alone with you.

00:46:13.450 --> 00:46:17.200
But what you're going through right now after losing your father...

00:46:17.200 --> 00:46:20.260
I understand that really well.

00:46:20.640 --> 00:46:23.520
And I don't want our relationship to remain so uncer tain.

00:46:24.230 --> 00:46:25.660
Our relationship?

00:46:26.680 --> 00:46:28.520
We have no relationship anymore.

00:46:29.330 --> 00:46:32.430
It was battle that brought us together,

00:46:32.430 --> 00:46:35.210
and that battle is now over.

00:46:35.210 --> 00:46:37.280
You really think it's over?

00:46:37.930 --> 00:46:41.840
Both our objective and the enemies we were targeting are gone.

00:46:41.840 --> 00:46:43.790
What do we have left to f ight for?

00:46:44.970 --> 00:46:48.210
Ever ything we believed was a lie, and—

00:46:48.210 --> 00:46:50.470
And you couldn't protect the one person you wanted to.

00:46:50.470 --> 00:46:52.540
T hat's what you're really thinking, isn't it?

00:46:52.940 --> 00:46:55.550
You never wanted to f ix the Kirijou Group's mistakes!

00:46:55.860 --> 00:46:59.270
All you ever wanted was to protect your father !

00:46:59.270 --> 00:47:00.800
T hat's the real reason you fought , right?

00:47:00.800 --> 00:47:02.300
Yes, it was!

00:47:02.610 --> 00:47:08.310
Ever since the accident , my father's had the face of a man dead inside!

00:47:08.600 --> 00:47:12.840
Like he thought he had no right to be alive after what he'd done!

00:47:12.840 --> 00:47:16.820
I fought so he'd never have to look like that again!

00:47:17.160 --> 00:47:20.600
But you saw what a joke that turned out to be!

00:47:20.600 --> 00:47:23.330
I was right next to Ikutsuki the entire time!

00:47:23.690 --> 00:47:26.080
And yet I fell into his trap, unable to do a single thing!

00:47:27.080 --> 00:47:28.580
It was all for nothing in the end.

00:47:29.710 --> 00:47:32.830
I may as well not have been there!

00:47:40.550 --> 00:47:41.590
I'm sorr y.

00:47:41.960 --> 00:47:44.600
But we don't know if it was all for nothing yet !

00:47:45.180 --> 00:47:46.230
Takeba...

00:47:46.230 --> 00:47:50.200
Remember that video of the accident we watched in Yakushima?

00:47:50.200 --> 00:47:51.250
It was a fake.

00:47:52.100 --> 00:47:57.670
Ikutsuki tampered with it so that it would back up his stor y.

00:47:57.670 --> 00:48:01.060
Fuuka found the original recording not too long ago,

00:48:01.060 --> 00:48:02.110
and I watched it .

00:48:02.770 --> 00:48:07.120
<i>My employer become obsessed with a loathsome idea.</i>

00:48:07.500 --> 00:48:10.260
<i>T his experiment should have never even been conceived!</i>

00:48:10.260 --> 00:48:13.630
<i>T hat's why I had to interrupt it .</i>

00:48:14.200 --> 00:48:16.620
<i>Please, listen carefully.</i>

00:48:16.620 --> 00:48:18.630
<i>I cannot stress this enough.</i>

00:48:18.950 --> 00:48:20.630
<i>Do not hunt the scattered Shadows!</i>

00:48:22.030 --> 00:48:25.140
<i>T hey're tr ying to consume one another and reunite as one.</i>

00:48:25.620 --> 00:48:28.560
<i>But if they're reunited, we're all doomed!</i>

00:48:29.640 --> 00:48:31.190
<i>I'll say this once more.</i>

00:48:31.190 --> 00:48:33.650
<i>Leave the Shadows be!</i>

00:48:34.480 --> 00:48:39.190
My dad tried to prevent the disaster he saw coming.

00:48:39.190 --> 00:48:41.330
He never, ever gave up.

00:48:41.330 --> 00:48:42.900
He put his life on the line until the end.

00:48:43.750 --> 00:48:46.410
T hat's why I've decided to f ight .

00:48:47.410 --> 00:48:50.410
I want to continue f ighting to end the Dark Hour.

00:48:51.100 --> 00:48:53.170
I want to f ight to carr y out my dad's will.

00:48:53.770 --> 00:48:55.340
Carr y out his will?

00:48:55.340 --> 00:48:56.830
T hat's all I—

00:48:56.830 --> 00:49:01.600
No, that's all <i>we</i> can do for them, Mitsuru.

00:49:01.600 --> 00:49:02.710
Takeba...

00:49:07.300 --> 00:49:09.220
You're right .

00:49:09.220 --> 00:49:11.310
Nothing's over yet .

00:49:12.250 --> 00:49:14.810
So I'll have to see this through to the end.

00:49:15.530 --> 00:49:17.490
For my father in Heaven,

00:49:17.490 --> 00:49:18.820
and for you as well.

00:49:18.820 --> 00:49:20.320
Mitsuru!

00:49:20.840 --> 00:49:24.340
Will you f ight alongside me, Yukari?

00:49:35.230 --> 00:49:37.330
We're here!

00:49:37.330 --> 00:49:39.090
T his is one nice inn!

00:49:39.810 --> 00:49:42.590
I see a stony, outdoor area f illed with water.

00:49:42.930 --> 00:49:46.090
Is that the fabled "open-air bath"?

00:49:46.460 --> 00:49:49.250
No, that's just a decorative garden.

00:49:49.250 --> 00:49:51.510
You'd be exposed for the whole lobby to see.

00:49:51.510 --> 00:49:52.930
I see.

00:49:53.660 --> 00:49:54.950
Oh, yeah!

00:49:54.950 --> 00:49:58.840
Where was your old school gonna take their class trip, Ryouji?

00:49:58.840 --> 00:50:01.860
My old school, huh?

00:50:03.780 --> 00:50:04.770
Where was it now?

00:50:04.770 --> 00:50:06.470
You seriously don't remember!?

00:50:06.470 --> 00:50:08.870
Who doesn't remember something so major?

00:50:09.170 --> 00:50:10.850
So boys down the hall?

00:50:10.850 --> 00:50:12.900
And the girls upstairs.

00:50:12.900 --> 00:50:14.620
We'll see you later, then!

00:50:14.620 --> 00:50:17.620
Seriously ! Stop following us already.

00:50:17.620 --> 00:50:19.130
Boys down the hall!

00:50:19.460 --> 00:50:20.940
You're up here, Aigis!

00:50:22.210 --> 00:50:24.180
Where's Makoto?

00:50:24.180 --> 00:50:26.000
He was just here.

00:50:26.000 --> 00:50:27.570
Again?

00:50:27.570 --> 00:50:29.390
Sheesh, what's with that guy ?

00:50:29.690 --> 00:50:31.610
T hat's kind of cold.

00:50:31.610 --> 00:50:34.170
Aren't you guys dormmates?

00:50:34.170 --> 00:50:35.930
Well, yeah, but ...

00:50:35.930 --> 00:50:38.650
I don't know what's been going through his head lately.

00:50:38.960 --> 00:50:42.140
He's struggling with his own good nature.

00:50:42.830 --> 00:50:44.540
He's too kind for his own good.

00:50:44.540 --> 00:50:47.870
Kind enough to be hopelessly awkward.

00:50:47.870 --> 00:50:53.160
So to keep anyone from getting hur t ,
he's built a wall around himself.

00:50:53.990 --> 00:50:58.920
A wall so tall that nobody can overcome it ver y easily.

00:50:58.920 --> 00:51:03.410
But the truth is, he built that wall to protect ever yone.

00:51:03.410 --> 00:51:06.090
You sure get how he works.

00:51:06.090 --> 00:51:06.920
Yep.

00:51:06.920 --> 00:51:08.930
I know him like I know myself.

00:51:09.300 --> 00:51:10.720
He's just awkward, huh?

00:51:10.720 --> 00:51:12.960
So don't be too harsh, okay ?

00:51:12.960 --> 00:51:15.680
Man, you're one tough cookie.

00:51:17.180 --> 00:51:20.190
Kyoto is an amazing place!

00:51:20.190 --> 00:51:21.690
I'd come back here in a hear tbeat !

00:51:22.690 --> 00:51:23.690
Hey.

00:51:25.790 --> 00:51:27.350
Come with me.

00:51:33.790 --> 00:51:35.160
What's wrong?

00:51:35.160 --> 00:51:36.960
You're doing nothing but defending.

00:51:36.960 --> 00:51:39.350
If you don't attack, you'll never win.

00:51:41.540 --> 00:51:43.710
Defending is cer tainly impor tant .

00:51:43.710 --> 00:51:46.210
But isn't it more impor tant to f ind something wor th defending?

00:51:46.790 --> 00:51:49.170
What good is a life with nothing to risk it over?

00:51:49.970 --> 00:51:53.680
Sure, it hur ts losing something so precious.

00:51:54.150 --> 00:51:56.460
I know that all too well.

00:51:56.460 --> 00:51:58.930
You never change, do you?

00:52:00.880 --> 00:52:06.190
You always go off and do whatever you want without a word to anyone.

00:52:06.860 --> 00:52:08.940
Put yourself in my shoes for a change.

00:52:09.760 --> 00:52:11.450
You think I'm one to talk, huh?

00:52:12.340 --> 00:52:14.290
I guess you're right .

00:52:14.290 --> 00:52:18.950
I was the one who kept self ishly rushing off on my own in search of power.

00:52:19.430 --> 00:52:20.850
Ever since my sister—

00:52:20.850 --> 00:52:25.090
Ever since Miki died, I've done nothing but tr y to get stronger.

00:52:25.090 --> 00:52:28.210
I thought if I was strong enough,
I could protect anything with my own hands.

00:52:29.080 --> 00:52:30.720
But look where we are now!

00:52:31.250 --> 00:52:33.220
Even you moved on without me!

00:52:33.850 --> 00:52:36.220
It's like you're laughing at my desperation!

00:52:36.950 --> 00:52:39.720
I knew that battle carried the risk of death.

00:52:40.860 --> 00:52:45.480
But I was so obsessed with f ighting that I failed to see anything else!

00:52:45.480 --> 00:52:48.460
It didn't matter how strong I was!

00:52:50.330 --> 00:52:52.490
It still ended in this mess.

00:52:58.000 --> 00:52:59.230
Um, Akihiko?

00:53:00.170 --> 00:53:01.970
T hat's just how it is.

00:53:01.970 --> 00:53:05.000
You never realize the value of something until you lose it .

00:53:05.400 --> 00:53:10.000
Even so, it's a million times better to hold something dear and lose it than to live as an empty shell.

00:53:11.000 --> 00:53:13.510
No matter how much it hur ts.

00:53:16.810 --> 00:53:18.010
Welcome back!

00:53:18.010 --> 00:53:20.260
Yo! Want some?

00:53:20.260 --> 00:53:21.020
What is it?

00:53:21.020 --> 00:53:23.200
A midnight snack, of course!

00:53:23.200 --> 00:53:26.510
Only losers would sleep during a class trip!

00:53:26.510 --> 00:53:27.640
He's right , you know!

00:53:27.640 --> 00:53:30.530
So we're not going to waste our time sleeping, right?

00:53:40.830 --> 00:53:42.540
Inf iltration successful.

00:53:42.840 --> 00:53:44.580
What are you doing here, Aigis?

00:53:44.580 --> 00:53:48.540
I deemed it unreasonable that Makoto and I were not in the same room.

00:53:49.130 --> 00:53:51.970
Ryouji, please switch rooms with me.

00:53:51.970 --> 00:53:54.290
I get to sleep in the girls' room? Really ?

00:53:54.290 --> 00:53:55.790
No way in hell!

00:53:55.790 --> 00:53:57.550
I would die of jealousy !

00:53:57.890 --> 00:53:59.820
Please feel free to join him.

00:53:59.820 --> 00:54:01.660
What , really !?

00:54:01.660 --> 00:54:02.960
W-Wait !

00:54:02.960 --> 00:54:04.310
Why the window?

00:54:04.310 --> 00:54:06.310
Can't we just use the door?

00:54:06.310 --> 00:54:07.430
No, you cannot .

00:54:07.430 --> 00:54:09.310
Hold on, Aigis.

00:54:09.650 --> 00:54:10.820
It's too narrow!

00:54:11.090 --> 00:54:13.280
T here's no way we can climb across these balconies!

00:54:13.280 --> 00:54:15.320
I had no trouble with it .

00:54:15.320 --> 00:54:17.570
Yeah, but we're not like you!

00:54:17.570 --> 00:54:19.270
Wait ! I'm falling!

00:54:19.270 --> 00:54:19.820
Ryouji!

00:54:22.020 --> 00:54:22.830
Makoto!

00:54:23.180 --> 00:54:24.330
Aigis!

00:54:33.890 --> 00:54:35.640
What was that sound just now?

00:54:35.640 --> 00:54:37.090
No clue.

00:54:40.170 --> 00:54:40.590
Cold! Too cold!

00:54:40.590 --> 00:54:41.850
Towel!
Cold! Too cold!

00:54:41.850 --> 00:54:43.350
Gimme hot water !

00:54:49.450 --> 00:54:50.360
Makoto?

00:55:20.890 --> 00:55:24.000
T his hot spring is supposed to make your biceps grow.

00:55:24.000 --> 00:55:29.460
Apparently this hot spring is used by both men and women at different times.

00:55:29.460 --> 00:55:31.190
Oh, really ?

00:55:31.190 --> 00:55:33.590
Maybe it'll change over while we're still in here.

00:55:33.590 --> 00:55:36.630
It wouldn't be our fault if that happened, right?

00:55:36.630 --> 00:55:37.760
Come on, you two!

00:55:37.760 --> 00:55:38.650
Shh!

00:55:39.030 --> 00:55:40.660
Someone's coming.

00:55:41.040 --> 00:55:43.660
All right ! No one's here!

00:55:43.660 --> 00:55:45.410
It's all ours!

00:55:45.410 --> 00:55:47.410
Wow, it's even bigger than I thought it was!

00:55:47.830 --> 00:55:51.420
None of the benef icial proper ties of this hot spring apply to me.

00:55:52.070 --> 00:55:53.760
I will request that they expand its features.

00:55:54.420 --> 00:55:56.850
Oh, shit ! It's them!

00:55:56.850 --> 00:55:58.390
Why are they here right now!?

00:55:58.390 --> 00:56:00.910
Ooh, Yukari and Fuuka!

00:56:00.910 --> 00:56:02.930
We sure are lucky—

00:56:03.380 --> 00:56:05.180
Are you suicidal, Ryouji!?

00:56:05.980 --> 00:56:06.680
Who's there!?

00:56:07.140 --> 00:56:08.370
Is someone over there!?

00:56:08.370 --> 00:56:09.480
What is it , Yukari?

00:56:09.480 --> 00:56:10.540
Did you see something?

00:56:11.590 --> 00:56:13.440
Mitsuru's here too!?

00:56:13.440 --> 00:56:14.610
Listen...

00:56:14.610 --> 00:56:16.770
If the times changed over, we're dead meat !

00:56:16.770 --> 00:56:20.120
But it was def initely men's turn when we came in.

00:56:20.120 --> 00:56:21.950
You think they'd let it slide as a bad joke?

00:56:21.950 --> 00:56:25.140
Do you honestly think she'd buy that lame excuse!?

00:56:25.140 --> 00:56:26.630
If we're found here...

00:56:26.630 --> 00:56:27.950
What'll happen?

00:56:27.950 --> 00:56:29.580
We'll be executed.

00:56:29.580 --> 00:56:31.290
E-Executed!?

00:56:34.350 --> 00:56:36.980
I'm sure I heard something.

00:56:36.980 --> 00:56:38.390
Really ?

00:56:38.390 --> 00:56:39.710
I'll check it out .

00:56:40.150 --> 00:56:41.220
T hey're coming!

00:56:42.330 --> 00:56:44.820
T he odds are against us, but we'll make do.

00:56:44.820 --> 00:56:46.100
Time to star t our mission!

00:56:46.100 --> 00:56:46.970
Mission?

00:56:47.590 --> 00:56:49.560
A mission to see another day.

00:56:49.560 --> 00:56:51.440
Failure means a swift death.

00:56:51.440 --> 00:56:53.240
R-Roger that .

00:56:53.240 --> 00:56:55.680
Let's all make it out together !

00:56:58.580 --> 00:57:00.070
Is someone there?

00:57:11.030 --> 00:57:14.000
If we can swim over there undetected, we're as good as gone.

00:57:14.520 --> 00:57:15.220
We're up for it , right?

00:57:15.220 --> 00:57:17.650
T hat's the back entrance, isn't it?

00:57:17.650 --> 00:57:20.000
I think the only way back in is through the banquet hall.

00:57:20.350 --> 00:57:22.510
Far better than being found by Mitsuru!

00:57:26.350 --> 00:57:27.510
A-Aigis.

00:57:27.830 --> 00:57:30.260
T hat's not how you bathe in a hot spring.

00:57:39.560 --> 00:57:41.590
T hat was a close call!

00:57:41.590 --> 00:57:42.670
And now,

00:57:42.670 --> 00:57:44.030
our escape!

00:57:47.040 --> 00:57:48.030
Junpei?

00:57:48.370 --> 00:57:49.170
What's wrong?

00:57:49.170 --> 00:57:50.240
Hurr y and get out here!

00:57:50.240 --> 00:57:52.720
I think this is the end of the line for me.

00:57:52.720 --> 00:57:54.540
You guys should go on without me.

00:57:54.830 --> 00:57:56.520
What are you saying?

00:57:56.520 --> 00:57:58.020
We're not leaving without you!

00:57:58.020 --> 00:57:58.660
Come on!

00:57:58.660 --> 00:58:00.550
I can't !

00:58:01.300 --> 00:58:02.660
Junpei...

00:58:02.660 --> 00:58:04.050
So you really...

00:58:04.470 --> 00:58:05.970
I lost ...

00:58:05.970 --> 00:58:08.550
I lost my towel!

00:58:09.050 --> 00:58:10.550
You idiot !

00:58:10.560 --> 00:58:12.640
Forget about me and go!

00:58:12.640 --> 00:58:14.310
It's either me or all of us!

00:58:14.310 --> 00:58:16.820
You think we could just leave you behind!?

00:58:16.820 --> 00:58:18.040
Junpei, look!

00:58:18.040 --> 00:58:18.810
A leaf !

00:58:19.140 --> 00:58:20.150
You can use a leaf !

00:58:20.150 --> 00:58:21.320
Don't mock me!

00:58:21.730 --> 00:58:23.870
Don't give up, Junpei!

00:58:23.870 --> 00:58:26.320
Didn't we vow we'd survive together?

00:58:28.250 --> 00:58:29.070
I'm sorr y.

00:58:31.490 --> 00:58:34.740
<i>Am I still unable to protect anyone!?</i>

00:58:34.740 --> 00:58:36.580
Who's back there!?

00:58:47.260 --> 00:58:48.940
D-Don't jump to conclusions!

00:58:48.940 --> 00:58:50.160
We can explain!

00:58:50.160 --> 00:58:51.350
S-Silence!

00:58:51.690 --> 00:58:53.100
Off with their heads!

00:58:53.570 --> 00:58:55.100
Aigis...

00:58:55.570 --> 00:58:57.350
It is a shame we must par t so soon.

00:58:57.350 --> 00:58:58.930
W-Wait !

00:58:58.930 --> 00:59:00.350
Seriously, stop! Please!

00:59:10.480 --> 00:59:13.430
I'll never forget yesterday.

00:59:13.430 --> 00:59:16.200
I'll never forget no matter how much I want to!

00:59:16.200 --> 00:59:17.530
It was a nightmare.

00:59:17.530 --> 00:59:19.620
An execution is exactly right .

00:59:20.150 --> 00:59:22.140
It was a nightmare.

00:59:22.140 --> 00:59:23.630
Do your best to forget .

00:59:43.680 --> 00:59:45.270
Is that a gift for someone?

00:59:45.270 --> 00:59:49.150
Yeah, but I'm not sure which one to go with.

00:59:49.980 --> 00:59:52.390
It's hard to pick just one.

00:59:52.390 --> 00:59:54.160
Is it for your girlfriend?

00:59:54.160 --> 00:59:55.800
Well, um...

00:59:55.800 --> 00:59:58.160
Yeah, I guess you could call her that .

00:59:58.160 --> 00:59:59.580
Maybe!

01:00:01.100 --> 01:00:04.260
Junpei looks like he's having fun.

01:00:04.260 --> 01:00:05.910
It's good he's having fun.

01:00:05.910 --> 01:00:08.420
Hairpins <i>do</i> make good gifts for girls.

01:00:08.860 --> 01:00:10.420
Guess I'll do the same!

01:00:11.590 --> 01:00:13.430
How many girls are buying for!?

01:00:21.810 --> 01:00:24.440
Junpei's coming back tomorrow.

01:00:28.100 --> 01:00:28.980
What?

01:00:28.980 --> 01:00:30.440
Why...

01:00:30.440 --> 01:00:31.700
It hur ts...

01:00:31.700 --> 01:00:33.220
Ow!

01:00:33.220 --> 01:00:34.950
It hur ts...

01:00:34.950 --> 01:00:35.950
I'm scared...

01:00:36.820 --> 01:00:37.950
Why ?

01:00:43.730 --> 01:00:44.870
What !?

01:00:44.870 --> 01:00:46.470
It's been a while.

01:00:47.590 --> 01:00:48.800
T hat voice is...

01:00:50.900 --> 01:00:53.400
I'm so glad we're able to meet again.

01:00:53.400 --> 01:00:56.140
Jin, give them to her.

01:00:59.750 --> 01:01:03.380
Now there's no reason for you to stay captive here any longer, no?

01:01:03.380 --> 01:01:04.400
Takaya...

01:01:04.940 --> 01:01:06.770
You understand, don't you?

01:01:06.770 --> 01:01:08.400
T here's no place for you here.

01:01:08.900 --> 01:01:10.910
T he only place you have is with us.

01:01:12.280 --> 01:01:16.910
You should already know that death is not a thing to be feared.

01:01:17.650 --> 01:01:19.910
T he only thing to fear is...

01:01:31.970 --> 01:01:34.180
I know, Takaya.

01:01:34.640 --> 01:01:35.930
Good girl.

01:01:38.390 --> 01:01:41.170
Yes, it's all his fault .

01:01:41.170 --> 01:01:45.440
I only star ted feeling this unbearable suffering again once he came.

01:01:46.510 --> 01:01:48.500
And I never feared death either.

01:02:05.460 --> 01:02:07.210
Farewell, Kyoto!

01:02:07.780 --> 01:02:09.090
It sure was fun.

01:02:09.090 --> 01:02:10.710
We made some good memories, huh?

01:02:11.830 --> 01:02:13.210
Yeah, we did.

01:02:13.940 --> 01:02:16.300
Phew, I'm beat !

01:02:16.300 --> 01:02:19.010
You're all so lucky !

01:02:19.010 --> 01:02:20.220
I wish I could've gone too.

01:02:21.430 --> 01:02:24.260
We bought you some souvenirs, so hang on!

01:02:24.260 --> 01:02:26.630
Koromaru, we brought you some spoils—

01:02:26.630 --> 01:02:29.190
I mean, souvenirs, as well.

01:02:30.340 --> 01:02:32.610
Where'd Junpei go?

01:02:32.610 --> 01:02:33.990
He went straight to the hospital.

01:02:34.580 --> 01:02:36.990
He said he wanted to give her his gift .

01:02:37.970 --> 01:02:39.530
Chidorin!

01:02:57.240 --> 01:02:58.010
Still nothing!?

01:02:58.500 --> 01:03:00.150
Hurr y and f ind her !

01:03:00.150 --> 01:03:02.080
Calm down, Junpei.

01:03:02.080 --> 01:03:04.100
You'll distract Yamagishi.

01:03:05.580 --> 01:03:06.400
Damn it !

01:03:06.400 --> 01:03:08.830
Where did you go, Chidori?

01:03:08.830 --> 01:03:10.770
It'll be okay, Junpei.

01:03:11.370 --> 01:03:13.770
Fuuka will def initely f ind her.

01:03:14.260 --> 01:03:15.530
T hen why...

01:03:15.530 --> 01:03:18.030
Why do I have such a bad feeling?

01:03:18.720 --> 01:03:19.780
Junpei.

01:03:21.580 --> 01:03:22.280
I found her !

01:03:22.980 --> 01:03:24.340
She's in front of Tar tarus!

01:03:34.160 --> 01:03:35.300
Chidori!

01:03:35.700 --> 01:03:37.150
What are you doing!?

01:03:38.340 --> 01:03:42.050
You know you shouldn't be out of the hospital yet !

01:03:42.580 --> 01:03:44.630
Let's go back together !

01:03:44.630 --> 01:03:45.460
Okay ?

01:03:46.530 --> 01:03:48.060
Watch out , Junpei!

01:03:58.330 --> 01:03:59.570
Chidori...

01:03:59.570 --> 01:04:01.320
All of you...

01:04:01.320 --> 01:04:03.710
You're all eyesores.

01:04:03.710 --> 01:04:05.340
I will erase you.

01:04:05.340 --> 01:04:07.000
What are you saying!?

01:04:07.000 --> 01:04:07.740
Come on!

01:04:07.740 --> 01:04:10.420
Snap out of it , Chidori!

01:04:10.420 --> 01:04:13.120
We're not enemies, right !?

01:04:13.120 --> 01:04:14.790
Get back, Junpei!

01:04:14.790 --> 01:04:15.840
She's dangerous!

01:04:16.340 --> 01:04:17.540
Persona!

01:04:22.090 --> 01:04:23.340
Chidori...

01:04:23.590 --> 01:04:25.010
We have to f ight back!

01:04:25.010 --> 01:04:26.460
Prepare yourselves!

01:04:26.460 --> 01:04:27.600
Iori!

01:04:27.600 --> 01:04:30.100
It's do or die now!

01:04:30.540 --> 01:04:32.100
Why ?

01:04:32.740 --> 01:04:34.070
Why are you doing this!?

01:04:48.380 --> 01:04:49.870
Polydeuces!

01:04:53.250 --> 01:04:54.750
Stop!

01:04:57.510 --> 01:04:58.680
What are you doing!?

01:04:58.680 --> 01:04:59.940
Please, stop!

01:04:59.940 --> 01:05:01.260
Chidori's not like this!

01:05:01.830 --> 01:05:03.000
She's not like this!

01:05:03.000 --> 01:05:04.760
Takaya was right .

01:05:04.760 --> 01:05:06.530
You're a nuisance!

01:05:09.970 --> 01:05:11.480
Sanada, look out !

01:05:45.160 --> 01:05:45.970
Koromaru!

01:05:45.970 --> 01:05:46.550
No, Koromaru!

01:05:49.940 --> 01:05:52.310
Attack mode: covering f ire!

01:05:57.990 --> 01:05:58.810
Chidori!

01:06:01.460 --> 01:06:02.570
Physical pain...

01:06:04.340 --> 01:06:07.570
is nothing compared to the unbearable hear tache.

01:06:07.900 --> 01:06:09.070
Arahabaki!

01:06:18.080 --> 01:06:19.290
No more.

01:06:19.290 --> 01:06:21.340
I can't stand here and watch this!

01:06:21.640 --> 01:06:22.610
Junpei?

01:06:22.610 --> 01:06:24.320
Please, ever yone!

01:06:24.320 --> 01:06:26.150
Let me handle this.

01:06:26.150 --> 01:06:27.890
T his is my battle to f ight !

01:06:27.890 --> 01:06:29.110
No, Junpei!

01:06:29.110 --> 01:06:30.350
It's too risky !

01:06:30.350 --> 01:06:32.470
Do you have a death wish, Iori!?

01:06:32.470 --> 01:06:34.070
Me, lie down and die!?

01:06:34.070 --> 01:06:36.150
And turn Chidori into a murderer!?

01:06:36.150 --> 01:06:37.350
No way in hell!

01:06:37.880 --> 01:06:39.140
What do you want?

01:06:39.140 --> 01:06:41.410
Chidori, enough already !

01:06:41.410 --> 01:06:42.360
You don't want to do this!

01:06:42.970 --> 01:06:45.110
Why should the two of us f ight? It's wrong!

01:06:45.330 --> 01:06:47.200
It's not wrong!

01:06:47.200 --> 01:06:50.870
I don't belong with you!

01:06:51.190 --> 01:06:52.870
I've known that from the ver y star t !

01:07:01.070 --> 01:07:02.180
Junpei!

01:07:03.380 --> 01:07:05.940
What are you doing, Akihiko?

01:07:05.940 --> 01:07:08.130
I know he's an idiot , but he's still a man!

01:07:08.710 --> 01:07:10.770
Let him tr y before we stomp on his pride.

01:07:10.770 --> 01:07:11.890
Akihiko?

01:07:12.330 --> 01:07:13.660
Come on!

01:07:13.660 --> 01:07:15.620
Why won't you attack?

01:07:15.620 --> 01:07:17.250
You should just kill me!

01:07:17.250 --> 01:07:18.640
Kill me!

01:07:26.910 --> 01:07:27.810
Junpei!

01:07:27.810 --> 01:07:29.910
I can't kill you.

01:07:30.170 --> 01:07:32.410
I could never kill you!

01:07:32.780 --> 01:07:33.890
Why not !?

01:07:33.890 --> 01:07:35.660
I'm not afraid to die!

01:07:41.670 --> 01:07:44.170
What I fear isn't death.

01:07:49.650 --> 01:07:51.300
What I fear is...

01:07:51.300 --> 01:07:53.190
What I fear most is...

01:07:53.190 --> 01:07:55.180
I fear attachment .

01:07:55.740 --> 01:07:58.310
I fear that once I grow attached to something, I'll lose it .

01:07:59.330 --> 01:08:02.690
Be it to things, my own life, or anything else.

01:08:03.310 --> 01:08:08.010
T hat's why we need to live only for the ver y moment !

01:08:08.010 --> 01:08:09.520
But you...

01:08:09.520 --> 01:08:11.700
You brought me pain I never asked for !

01:08:16.320 --> 01:08:17.430
Chidori...

01:08:18.360 --> 01:08:20.520
When I'm with you, Junpei,

01:08:20.520 --> 01:08:23.640
I star t fearing ever ything.

01:08:23.640 --> 01:08:25.460
I star t fearing loss.

01:08:26.370 --> 01:08:28.460
I star t fearing even death.

01:08:32.140 --> 01:08:35.720
I fear that our time together will come to an end.

01:08:37.720 --> 01:08:40.000
T hat's why I...

01:08:41.620 --> 01:08:44.230
I'm sorr y for making you feel afraid.

01:08:44.780 --> 01:08:47.470
But I'm the same way.

01:08:47.470 --> 01:08:48.980
I'm scared of losing you too.

01:08:48.980 --> 01:08:54.990
Nothing scares me more than the thought of not being able to be with you anymore.

01:08:55.500 --> 01:08:57.170
T hat's why...

01:08:57.170 --> 01:08:59.440
T hat's why we should be together, don't you think?

01:09:02.260 --> 01:09:04.070
We're both scared to be alone.

01:09:04.610 --> 01:09:08.020
So we have to care for each other and keep that from happening.

01:09:08.020 --> 01:09:09.280
Junpei...

01:09:11.160 --> 01:09:12.200
Chidori...

01:09:16.060 --> 01:09:17.260
I see.

01:09:17.800 --> 01:09:19.510
I guess that makes sense.

01:09:19.510 --> 01:09:20.270
Makoto?

01:09:41.310 --> 01:09:42.630
Chidori...

01:09:42.630 --> 01:09:44.540
I see you are beyond help now.

01:09:45.120 --> 01:09:48.040
You've been poisoned by them.

01:09:48.350 --> 01:09:49.690
You bastards!

01:09:59.110 --> 01:10:01.310
He's not breathing!

01:10:02.830 --> 01:10:03.890
Junpei!

01:10:03.890 --> 01:10:05.310
No!

01:10:05.790 --> 01:10:08.530
Junpei...

01:10:08.530 --> 01:10:09.410
No...

01:10:09.410 --> 01:10:11.570
No!

01:10:20.500 --> 01:10:21.420
Chidori?

01:10:21.420 --> 01:10:23.930
You know, before I met you,

01:10:23.930 --> 01:10:27.830
I never realized what I wanted for myself.

01:10:28.770 --> 01:10:31.590
I want to be with you, Junpei.

01:10:32.950 --> 01:10:34.970
I want to be with you forever.

01:10:34.970 --> 01:10:38.550
Um, I, uh... I want to be with you too.

01:10:38.550 --> 01:10:40.730
But it could never last .

01:10:40.730 --> 01:10:42.350
We only have a little time before...

01:10:42.640 --> 01:10:44.130
Before what?

01:10:44.130 --> 01:10:46.720
We're different from you.

01:10:46.720 --> 01:10:49.860
Since the ver y moment I gained my power...

01:10:50.340 --> 01:10:52.490
My f inal day has been set in stone.

01:10:53.360 --> 01:10:57.110
It was only after I met you that I star ted
thinking death could be scar y.

01:10:57.390 --> 01:11:00.810
I realized that it meant we would never meet again.

01:11:01.510 --> 01:11:02.490
T hat's why...

01:11:04.030 --> 01:11:08.090
T hat's why you can't die here, Junpei.

01:11:17.880 --> 01:11:18.990
T his freak ...

01:11:18.990 --> 01:11:20.140
He's stronger than before!

01:11:22.080 --> 01:11:23.850
Impressive, isn't it?

01:11:23.850 --> 01:11:26.640
My strength grows even as we speak now!

01:11:32.080 --> 01:11:34.400
I f ind it endlessly amusing.

01:11:35.040 --> 01:11:42.410
Fate has decided that we, who have no
attachment to life, shall be the ones to live!

01:11:51.810 --> 01:11:53.420
<i>Her power is...</i>

01:11:57.570 --> 01:11:58.920
I thought I...

01:11:59.270 --> 01:12:00.790
<i>It's the opposite of mine.</i>

01:12:00.790 --> 01:12:01.680
Junpei!

01:12:02.490 --> 01:12:04.890
<i>Her Persona doesn't sense life.</i>

01:12:04.890 --> 01:12:06.940
<i>It emits life.</i>

01:12:06.940 --> 01:12:12.750
<i>But , in order to revive a person, she must ...</i>

01:12:15.750 --> 01:12:16.950
It worked.

01:12:19.820 --> 01:12:20.960
Chidori!

01:12:24.180 --> 01:12:27.980
I can hear the life pulsing through you.

01:12:27.980 --> 01:12:30.060
It won't stop beating.

01:12:30.710 --> 01:12:34.510
Now I'll live on inside of you.

01:12:35.650 --> 01:12:38.930
We'll be together forever.

01:12:41.210 --> 01:12:42.510
Hey, Chidori!

01:12:42.510 --> 01:12:43.720
Stay with me!

01:12:44.210 --> 01:12:45.390
What are you saying!?

01:12:45.390 --> 01:12:46.470
Hey !

01:12:46.470 --> 01:12:50.480
I'll protect you now, Junpei.

01:12:50.840 --> 01:12:51.980
Always.

01:12:53.600 --> 01:12:54.480
I will too!

01:12:54.480 --> 01:12:56.740
I'll protect you too!

01:12:56.740 --> 01:12:57.420
So please!

01:12:57.420 --> 01:13:01.320
It feels so nice to be with you.

01:13:01.320 --> 01:13:02.240
Chidori!

01:13:03.560 --> 01:13:06.340
I love you, Junpei.

01:13:08.010 --> 01:13:09.330
T hank you...

01:13:13.590 --> 01:13:14.880
Chidori?

01:13:15.670 --> 01:13:17.000
T his can't be real.

01:13:17.440 --> 01:13:18.380
Chidori!

01:13:18.380 --> 01:13:19.700
Wake up!

01:13:19.700 --> 01:13:20.760
Answer me!

01:13:21.390 --> 01:13:24.240
Chidori!

01:13:24.890 --> 01:13:25.760
Junpei?

01:13:31.110 --> 01:13:32.270
What a pity.

01:13:32.560 --> 01:13:35.630
What a meaningless death.

01:13:36.400 --> 01:13:37.900
"Meaningless"?

01:13:55.120 --> 01:13:56.290
It changed!?

01:13:56.590 --> 01:13:58.290
You'll pay for this!

01:14:12.810 --> 01:14:14.220
You little!

01:14:19.150 --> 01:14:20.070
You shall not !

01:14:20.320 --> 01:14:21.360
You piece of scrap!

01:14:30.010 --> 01:14:31.080
You're f inished!

01:14:42.820 --> 01:14:44.340
Makoto!

01:14:44.340 --> 01:14:45.340
At the end of the day,

01:14:45.830 --> 01:14:48.340
we're all alone in the world.

01:14:49.250 --> 01:14:50.340
T hat's not true.

01:14:56.000 --> 01:14:59.090
Why bother getting close to others?

01:14:59.090 --> 01:15:01.980
It only means that you'll be hur t when you lose them.

01:15:01.980 --> 01:15:02.860
T hat's not true!

01:15:03.140 --> 01:15:06.610
I'll blow you all to chunks in one shot !

01:15:09.300 --> 01:15:10.490
Mitsuru!

01:15:10.490 --> 01:15:12.620
I'm all right , Yukari.

01:15:13.400 --> 01:15:15.360
No matter how much you cherish something,

01:15:15.360 --> 01:15:17.830
once it's gone, that's the end of it .

01:15:18.620 --> 01:15:20.630
So it's better to never have anything at all.

01:15:21.830 --> 01:15:23.130
No, it's not !

01:15:23.400 --> 01:15:24.880
You don't need anything.

01:15:25.220 --> 01:15:26.630
I do!

01:15:30.640 --> 01:15:32.390
You don't want anything.

01:15:32.740 --> 01:15:34.050
I really do.

01:15:34.050 --> 01:15:35.100
I'm...

01:15:35.100 --> 01:15:37.830
I'm tired of running from getting close to others!

01:15:51.200 --> 01:15:53.410
What's this power!?

01:15:53.710 --> 01:15:55.660
It is all or nothing now!

01:15:56.190 --> 01:15:57.860
Orgia Drive activated!

01:16:11.850 --> 01:16:12.760
Shit !

01:16:12.760 --> 01:16:15.930
We shall retreat for now, Jin.

01:16:15.930 --> 01:16:17.330
Got it !

01:16:26.480 --> 01:16:28.850
Damn! We let them escape!

01:16:28.850 --> 01:16:29.990
Chidori.

01:16:43.080 --> 01:16:45.210
T his came from the hospital this morning.

01:16:45.940 --> 01:16:48.180
I thought that you should keep it , Iori.

01:16:52.150 --> 01:16:54.690
T hese are Chidori's drawings.

01:16:54.690 --> 01:16:56.220
What did she draw?

01:16:56.600 --> 01:16:59.000
Stuff you probably wouldn't understand.

01:16:59.000 --> 01:17:01.830
She drew stuff from out of this world.

01:17:06.970 --> 01:17:08.930
What's so hard to understand?

01:17:08.930 --> 01:17:09.990
T hat's amazing!

01:17:09.990 --> 01:17:12.400
Wow, what a beautiful por trait !

01:17:12.400 --> 01:17:14.660
It's a tad too flattering, though.

01:17:14.660 --> 01:17:20.250
I... I know things turned out like this,
but there's one thing I can say for sure.

01:17:21.050 --> 01:17:23.440
I'm glad I met Chidori.

01:17:24.660 --> 01:17:28.000
And I'm glad that I fell in love with her.

01:17:30.990 --> 01:17:32.130
I see.

01:17:52.420 --> 01:17:54.310
Yeah, it's good.

01:17:54.310 --> 01:17:55.770
Really good!

01:17:55.770 --> 01:17:57.110
Right?

01:17:57.110 --> 01:17:57.660
What?

01:17:58.180 --> 01:17:59.920
I was thinking that you'd changed.

01:17:59.920 --> 01:18:01.910
You come across a lot softer now.

01:18:02.420 --> 01:18:04.970
I've decided to accept it .

01:18:06.420 --> 01:18:07.700
Being friends, I mean.

01:18:07.700 --> 01:18:09.670
I'm happy to hear that .

01:18:12.410 --> 01:18:13.170
What's wrong?

01:18:13.760 --> 01:18:15.680
My head hur ts a little.

01:18:16.390 --> 01:18:18.570
I'm f ine. It's nothing, really.

01:18:21.620 --> 01:18:23.930
You found all this in Ikutsuki's study ?

01:18:24.340 --> 01:18:25.620
Yes.

01:18:25.620 --> 01:18:27.800
I've learned a lot from his f iles.

01:18:27.800 --> 01:18:31.690
It seems Ikutsuki had a hand in Strega too.

01:18:32.120 --> 01:18:33.270
T hese are...

01:18:34.990 --> 01:18:37.700
But we have something more pressing to deal with.

01:18:55.880 --> 01:18:57.470
What is this reaction?

01:19:10.300 --> 01:19:12.510
My past data recordings...

01:19:12.510 --> 01:19:13.730
are playing backwards.

01:19:16.410 --> 01:19:17.620
My memories...

01:19:18.550 --> 01:19:19.740
are returning.

01:19:32.680 --> 01:19:33.750
Oh, if it isn't ...

01:19:35.890 --> 01:19:38.830
I found myself here without realizing it .

01:19:38.830 --> 01:19:40.930
I don't really understand it myself.

01:19:40.930 --> 01:19:44.210
T he sky and ground are a strange color,

01:19:44.210 --> 01:19:46.270
and there's no one in sight .

01:19:46.850 --> 01:19:47.830
Have you forgotten?

01:19:49.490 --> 01:19:50.710
T he Dark Hour.

01:19:51.430 --> 01:19:54.100
A time period where ver y few are active.

01:19:54.100 --> 01:19:56.980
But you have somehow adapted to it .

01:19:56.980 --> 01:19:59.530
Far too well for an ordinar y human.

01:20:01.590 --> 01:20:04.030
<i>It is the time of awakening.</i>

01:20:04.320 --> 01:20:08.040
<i>A presence that has long slumbered is awakening tonight .</i>

01:20:08.860 --> 01:20:12.040
<i>It wakes to bring an end to the world.</i>

01:20:13.110 --> 01:20:14.040
An end?

01:20:14.420 --> 01:20:16.300
<i>You should already know all this.</i>

01:20:22.910 --> 01:20:24.530
What's this?

01:20:25.800 --> 01:20:28.150
It's all clearly documented here.

01:20:28.150 --> 01:20:30.060
T he twelve Shadows of the Arcana,

01:20:30.680 --> 01:20:33.800
and the being that comes after them.

01:20:33.800 --> 01:20:35.070
What being?

01:20:35.790 --> 01:20:38.280
T he end of the world that Ikutsuki mentioned...

01:20:39.310 --> 01:20:41.070
It was more than just mad babbling.

01:20:41.940 --> 01:20:44.180
It is all clear now.

01:20:44.180 --> 01:20:49.300
Now I understand the reason behind this feeling I sense when you're around.

01:20:49.300 --> 01:20:51.320
What do you mean?

01:20:51.320 --> 01:20:52.330
You are dangerous.

01:20:53.050 --> 01:20:55.090
You are my enemy.

01:20:55.500 --> 01:20:56.850
Me?

01:20:56.850 --> 01:20:59.090
Your enemy ?

01:20:59.540 --> 01:21:02.270
We have met once before.

01:21:02.270 --> 01:21:03.840
As adversaries.

01:21:04.170 --> 01:21:05.350
Who...

01:21:05.350 --> 01:21:08.170
Who am I?

01:21:08.170 --> 01:21:09.350
Who are you?

01:21:16.910 --> 01:21:18.830
I am Aigis.

01:21:18.830 --> 01:21:21.940
T he last remaining Anti-Shadow Emergency Control Weapon.

01:21:22.670 --> 01:21:25.430
A machine created to destroy Shadows.

01:21:26.510 --> 01:21:27.620
And you...

01:21:28.520 --> 01:21:31.720
When all twelve Shadows of the Arcana come together,

01:21:31.720 --> 01:21:34.420
they create the Shadow of the thir teenth Arcana.

01:21:34.420 --> 01:21:37.380
Its purpose it to bring about the end of the world, and it's name is...

01:21:38.340 --> 01:21:41.380
Your true name is "Death."

01:21:41.900 --> 01:21:45.100
You are the Shadow I sealed away ten years ago.

01:21:57.880 --> 01:21:58.770
I remember now.

01:21:59.810 --> 01:22:02.900
Who, and what , I am!

01:22:03.510 --> 01:22:04.570
Palladion!

01:22:08.410 --> 01:22:10.410
Stop this, Aigis!

01:22:25.250 --> 01:22:26.680
Aigis!

01:22:35.700 --> 01:22:37.560
Why...
